    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals are electropositive elements that lose electrons to form positive ions, whereas non-metals are electronegative elements.",
        "Most metals form basic oxides when combined with oxygen, whereas non-metals form acidic or neutral oxides.",
        "Oxides like Aluminium Oxide (Al2O3) and Zinc Oxide (ZnO) are amphoteric because they react with both acids and bases.",
        "Sodium and Potassium are extremely reactive metals stored under kerosene oil to prevent accidental fires.",
        "The reactivity series ranks metals in descending order of their chemical reactivity, with Potassium at the top and Gold at the bottom."
      ],
      "id": "t4w2375"
